# Calibration & data governance

## Ask before changing coefficients, tags, or weights

Before changing any of the following, **stop and ask the user**:

- numeric coefficients / multipliers / penalties / thresholds (Battle, Evaluation, tags, role-fit, etc.)
- custom tag membership, magnitudes, or effect shape
- axis weights / phase weights / `realWinRateWeight` and similar configs (`axis-weights.json`, hardcoded consts, etc.)

Do not “fix divergence” or “tune while here” by editing these without an explicit go-ahead.

OK without asking: bug fixes that restore an already-agreed value; copy/UI that does not change math; tests that assert existing behavior.

## Never recompute real-data pipelines without a request

Do **not** run scripts that refetch or recompute from live/external match data unless the user explicitly asks, including (non-exhaustive):

- `fetch-hero-meta` / `refetch-incomplete-hero-meta` / `recompute-presumed-positions`
- `fetch-pro-matches*` / hero-meta or pro-match refresh
- `calibrate-evaluation-values` / ability-tag aggregate pipelines that rewrite hero calibration
- any other OpenDota/Explorer/Liquipedia pull or full seed driven by a fresh external snapshot

Local `npm run seed` from **already present** data files is fine when needed to load existing snapshots into SQLite — still do not refresh those snapshots first without asking.
